      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A series of new κ opioid receptor (KOR) agonists were developed from the lead compound 4-dimethylamino-1-pentanoylpiperidine (3), a matrine-type alkaloid. Derivatives of 3 were synthesized with a variety of phenyl substituents and evaluated for their antinociceptive effects. Additionally, their selectivity for an opioid receptor was investigated for cis-4c and d, and trans-4g, all of which had high activity exerted through the KOR."},
